{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"GlaxoSmithKline, Medicines Research Centre, Stevenage, Hertfordshire SG1 2NY, United Kingdom."}]}},{"fullName":"Jakobsen BK","lastName":"Jakobsen","firstName":"Bent K","initials":"BK","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Immunocore, Ltd., Abingdon, Oxfordshire OX14 4RY, United Kingdom; and."}]}},{"fullName":"Vuidepot A","lastName":"Vuidepot","firstName":"Annelise","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Immunocore, Ltd., Abingdon, Oxfordshire OX14 4RY, United Kingdom; and."}]}},{"fullName":"Harper S","lastName":"Harper","firstName":"Stephen","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6029-8668"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Immunocore, Ltd., Abingdon, Oxfordshire OX14 4RY, United Kingdom; and Stephen.Harper@immunocore.com bent.jakobsen@immunocore.com."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1073-2091"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1482-0910"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5653-2271"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6029-8668"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8516-7787"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9303-639X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1928-208X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4525-7144"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4569-9276"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4715-4325"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-9734-2458"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","protocols"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"7","volume":"204","journalIssueId":2926607,"dateOfPublication":"2020 Apr","monthOfPublication":4,"yearOfPublication":2020,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Immunol","title":"Journal of immunology (Baltimore, Md. : 1950)","essn":"1550-6606","issn":"0022-1767","isoabbreviation":"J Immunol","nlmid":"2985117R"},"printPublicationDate":"2020-04-01"},"pubYear":"2020","pageInfo":"1943-1953","abstractText":"The molecular rules driving TCR cross-reactivity are poorly understood and, consequently, it is unclear the extent to which TCRs targeting the same Ag recognize the same off-target peptides. We determined TCR-peptide-HLA crystal structures and, using a single-chain peptide-HLA phage library, we generated peptide specificity profiles for three newly identified human TCRs specific for the cancer testis Ag NY-ESO-1<sub>157-165</sub>-HLA-A2. Two TCRs engaged the same central peptide feature, although were more permissive at peripheral peptide positions and, accordingly, possessed partially overlapping peptide specificity profiles. The third TCR engaged a flipped peptide conformation, leading to the recognition of off-target peptides sharing little similarity with the cognate peptide. These data show that TCRs specific for a cognate peptide recognize discrete peptide repertoires and reconciles how an individual's limited TCR repertoire following negative selection in the thymus is able to recognize a vastly larger antigenic pool.","affiliation":"Immunocore, Ltd., Abingdon, Oxfordshire OX14 4RY, United Kingdom; and.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Line"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Peptides","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Peptide Library"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Receptors, Antigen, T-Cell","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Histocompatibility Antigens","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"HLA-A2 Antigen","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Peptides","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Histocompatibility Antigens","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Receptors, Antigen, T-Cell","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"HLA-A2 Antigen","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Peptide Library","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.4049/jimmunol.1900915"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC7086387"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC7086387?pdf=render"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.4049/jimmunol.1900915"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":56,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["pdb"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2020-10-23","dateOfCreation":"2020-02-28","dateOfRevision":"2020-10-23","electronicPublicationDate":"2020-02-26","firstPublicationDate":"2020-02-26","firstIndexDate":"2020-02-28","fullTextReceivedDate":"2025-02-03","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}